WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.458 --> 00:00:03.878
[band plays national anthem]

00:00:04.379 --> 00:00:06.214
(speaker)
It's an honor to be here with
you all on this day

00:00:06.214 --> 00:00:08.633
to thank our veterans
to honor their sacrifices.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.552 size:88% position:44% line:76%
Many carry
the physical wounds of war

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:12.846 line:76%
almost all carry
the invisible scars.

00:00:12.887 --> 00:00:15.181 line:76%
They join the service
whole and often

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.392 line:76%
leave pieces of themselves
in these distant lands.

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:20.520
Yet they would never leave
a fallen brother behind.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.897
And they were driven to complete
the mission no matter what.

00:00:22.897 --> 00:00:24.315
An Army Ranger chooses this.

00:00:24.315 --> 00:00:25.608
He volunteers for it,

00:00:25.608 --> 00:00:27.986
fully knowing the hazards
of his chosen profession.

00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:30.739
It's not for the money, he makes
not much more than if he chose

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:33.491
a regular nine
to five non-combat job.

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:35.326
It's not for the benefits,
you get the same

00:00:35.326 --> 00:00:37.829
if you chose a less hazardous
specialty

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.540
It's not for the work
life balance,

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.667
He trains for seven months
and deploys for four months

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:45.044
every year, giving up time
with his family and loved ones.

00:00:45.795 --> 00:00:47.130
So why does he do it?

00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:49.924
He does it for the man to his
left and his right,

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:52.218
to protect his loved ones
back home,

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:54.262
for all of us
civilians stateside right now.

00:00:55.096 --> 00:00:56.598
Regardless of whether
you support him or not,

00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:59.058
he's willing to sacrifice
everything for you.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:01.311
Many have given
that ultimate sacrifice

00:01:01.311 --> 00:01:02.562
and may they never be forgotten.

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:05.106
To all
the veterans who have served,

00:01:05.106 --> 00:01:06.524
thank you for the sacrifices
you've made

00:01:06.524 --> 00:01:08.985
and continue to make,
you have given this country

00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:11.780
a privilege
that is beyond payment.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.199
We honor you for that today
and every day.

00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:15.909
Thank you.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:19.913
[applause]

